# Claude Code notes

`AGENTS.md` above is the contract. Everything in it applies to you exactly as
it applies to Codex. This file only covers what is specific to this runtime.

- When Claude Code loads the TAOS entries in `.claude/settings.json`,
  PreToolUse runs the guard and SessionStart shows the compact status. If
  the status did not appear, run the status command below. In a linked
  workspace, hooks may be skipped or may need the person's manual merge.
- If your runtime does not support the `@AGENTS.md` import on the first line,
  read `AGENTS.md` yourself before doing anything.
- Skills live in `.claude/skills/`. `taos-start` and `taos-handoff` cover the
  two flows you will use most.
- Use this command from the OS clone, a linked workspace, or its worktree.
  Keep the launcher, `--home`, and quotes as printed for later TAOS commands.

  ```bash
  {{taos_cli}} status --compact
  ```
